    "reducedMotion": "The machine never starts. The first phrase is rendered in full and stays — the final text state, immediately, rather than an empty slot or a sped-up cycle. The caret is still rendered but its own reduced-motion rule holds it solid.",
    "cleanup": "A single `window.clearTimeout(timer.current)` in the effect teardown. Only one timeout is ever outstanding, so no phase can survive unmount and call `setState` on a dead component.",
    "acceptance": "Watch one full cycle: the phrase erases visibly faster than the next one types — time it and the ratio is 2:1. At the empty string there is a perceptible pause before the next phrase starts. The caret holds solid while characters move and blinks while the phrase is held. Nothing to the right of the component moves at any point during the cycle. With reduced motion enabled the first phrase is present on first paint and never changes.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical"
