    "reducedMotion": "The cursor still appears, still inverts and still changes size — those are affordances, not motion. Both quickTo durations drop to 0 so the dot is welded to the pointer, and the fade in and out is instant. The CSS size transition is left in place; it is a 400ms state change, not continuous movement.",
    "cleanup": "Removes both container listeners, restores the container's original inline `cursor` value, resets the dot to `display: none`, then `gsap.killTweensOf` and `clearProps: \"all\"` to drop the two quickTo tweens and the centring transform. Nothing is left on the element for a remount to inherit.",
    "acceptance": "Move across the panel and a white dot follows a few frames behind, inverting the text and background under it — dark text goes light where the dot crosses it. Hover a link and it grows to 44px; hover a `data-cursor=\"view\"` target and it grows to 150px with a label that scales up inside it. During the growth the dot stays centred on the pointer and never lags further behind than it did at rest. Leave the panel and it fades out. On touch there is no dot at all and the native cursor is untouched.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical"
