    "cleanup": "The effect removes the capture-phase `click` listener with the same capture flag it was added with — passing `true` on the way out is required, since a listener added with capture is a different registration from one added without — removes the `pointerdown` listener, and calls `disarm()`, which clears the pending timeout and resets the flag so a remount does not start armed. No rAF, no pointer capture, nothing else held.",
    "acceptance": "Click a card: it opens, and the on-screen counter shows one activation and no swallow. Drag the row and release over a card: the row moves, the card does not open, and the swallow counter goes up by exactly one. Immediately click that same card: it opens — the swallow was consumed by the drag and did not carry over. Drag and release over the gap between cards, then click a card: it opens, because the arm expired instead of waiting for a click that never came. Tab to a card and press Enter, then Space: it opens both times, including immediately after a drag, and the swallow counter does not move. Put a real `<a href>` in the row and drag onto it: the page does not navigate.",
