    "reducedMotion": "No triggers are created and no `fromTo` runs, so every line renders at its final position and full opacity on first paint. The clipping boxes stay in the markup and do nothing, so the layout is byte-for-byte the finished state.",
    "cleanup": "`ctx.revert()` on unmount and on every dependency change: it kills each group's tween and ScrollTrigger and restores the inline `transform` and `opacity` GSAP wrote, so a re-mount measures clean markup rather than the last run's end state.",
    "acceptance": "Scroll the vertical section: the three lines rise out of their masks in sequence and reverse cleanly when you scroll back up. Keep scrolling into the pinned strip: each panel's lines rise with the same rhythm as it crosses the container, not as it crosses the viewport. With reduced motion on, every line is already in place.",
