    "cleanup": "Removes all four container listeners, calls `gsap.killTweensOf(proxy)` so no tween can write to a detached node after React releases it, then clears the inline `clipPath`, `transform` and `opacity` that `write()` set. The proxy is a local object and is garbage-collected with the closure.",
    "acceptance": "Move across the panel and a disc of the second layer drags along behind the pointer at a steady speed, with a thin ring exactly on its edge — no gap, no crescent of the base layer showing between them, even when you flick the pointer. Hover the trigger and the disc grows smoothly past the corners until the reveal layer fills the panel, with the ring fading out as it goes; leave and it shrinks back to the pointer. Resize the panel to a very wide or very tall aspect ratio and the disc stays circular and stays the same physical size. On touch the disc is parked left-of-centre and static.",
