    "reducedMotion": "The render loop never starts. One frame is drawn at a fixed time slice with the light parked at (0.34, 0.6), presence at 1 and energy at 0.35, so the panel is a composed still of the effect at rest rather than a flat rectangle. The pointer listener stays attached but its target is never read, so moving the cursor changes nothing.",
    "cleanup": "Removes the `pointermove` and `pointerleave` listeners from the canvas, nulls the stage ref so an in-flight frame cannot touch a disposed renderer, then calls `disposeRenderer` (which stops the animation loop, disposes the renderer and calls `forceContextLoss()` — `dispose()` alone leaves the context alive until GC decides otherwise, which may be never), disposes the geometry and the `ShaderMaterial`, and removes the canvas from the DOM. Because the canvas is created inside the effect, the StrictMode second run starts from a fresh element and a fresh context.",
    "acceptance": "Move the pointer across the panel and a soft light follows it with a short, even tail; the same tail length on a 60Hz and a 120Hz display. Move fast and the light brightens; stop and it settles to a dimmer ember without going out. Leave the panel and the light fades where it stands instead of sliding to the centre. The noise field keeps drifting slowly whether or not the pointer moves. White text over the glow core stays readable at any `glowGain`. Resize the container and the glow stays circular, not elliptical. In development, with StrictMode double-mounting, the canvas renders — it is not blank. With reduced motion the panel is a single composed still.",
