    "reducedMotion": "The rAF subscription is never made and both layers are drawn once at `elapsed` 0. That is a complete frame, not a collapsed one: the scatter, depths, sizes, tints and wrap fade are all per-particle seeds that already vary at t=0, so the still shows the same depth split, in front of and behind the same text, with only the drift absent. Resizing redraws the same still in both layers.",
    "cleanup": "Per layer: `geometry.remove()` deletes the VAOs and every buffer, `program.remove()` deletes the shaders and the program, `loseContext(gl)` hands the context back through `WEBGL_lose_context` — ogl has no `dispose()` and nothing else releases a context — then the canvas backing store is zeroed and the node removed. Both layers are torn down in the same cleanup, so the component never holds one context after the other has gone.",
    "acceptance": "Particles visibly pass both behind and in front of the text, and the text is still selectable with the mouse while they do. There is no horizontal line anywhere in the container where the field changes character. Near particles are larger, softer and move further per second than far ones. Links inside the content still respond to hover and click. Resize narrow and wide: discs stay circular and the population changes without a stutter. Two contexts per instance, both released on unmount — mount and unmount six instances and none of the earlier ones go black.",
