    "reducedMotion": "The reduced branch adopts the target scalars outright and lays the row out once, so the resolved geometry is on screen rather than a fast spread toward it. The frame loop is not subscribed at all, so no work is scheduled for a user who asked for none, and a later prop change still re-derives the layout immediately through the same code path. Because the layout is a pure function of the four scalars, the reduced render is pixel-identical to the settled animated one.",
