    "reducedMotion": "The ambient rotation freezes at 0.35 rad and the automatic firing cycle stops, so nothing moves unprompted. A pointer press still fires a full burst, because that is feedback for something the user did rather than decoration. The frame loop is subscribed only while a burst is actually in flight and unsubscribes as soon as the last particle lands, so the idle cost is zero.",
    "cleanup": "Removes the pointerdown listener, nulls the stage ref so a queued frame cannot touch a dead renderer, disposes the geometry via `disposeObject(scene)`, disposes the material, calls `disposeRenderer` for `dispose` + `forceContextLoss` + a zeroed backing store, and removes the canvas. `useRaf` unsubscribes on unmount, so a StrictMode double-invoke leaves no orphaned context.",
    "acceptance": "Concentric rings of dots turn slowly. Roughly every 1.5 seconds one sector throws a spray of brighter particles outward that fade as they travel, and the particles visibly do not move in lockstep — some shoot ahead and settle, others trail. Clicking a sector fires it immediately. The ring never develops a gap where a burst came from. With reduced motion the ring is still and nothing fires on its own, but a click still produces a full burst.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical"
