    "reducedMotion": "The overlay gets `display: none` and the click handler calls `onNavigate` synchronously, so navigation is a hard cut with no coloured frame in either direction. Not a zero-duration wipe — that is still one painted frame of full-bleed colour, which is a flash. The prefetch half is untouched, because a warm cache is not motion and is precisely the thing a visitor on a slow connection wants kept.",
    "cleanup": "Both delegated listeners are removed with the same `{ capture: true }` flag they were added with, or the removal silently fails to match. The `transitionend` listener and the safety timer are torn down together whenever the leaving state changes, the rAF that re-enables the transition after a bfcache restore is cancelled, and the `pageshow` listener is removed on unmount. Injected `<link rel=\"prefetch\">` tags are deliberately left in the head: removing a hint mid-flight cancels the fetch it exists to start.",
    "acceptance": "Hover a nav item and its dot lights — the href has been hinted, once, and hovering again does not re-hint. Click and the panel wipes over from the left in 0.4 s, the content swaps while covered, and the wipe retracts to the same edge with the opposite ease. Cmd-click, middle-click and a `download` link all behave like ordinary links with no wipe. On a real site, navigate away and press Back: the page appears with no leftover overlay and no reveal animation. With reduced motion the content swaps instantly and no coloured surface is ever painted.",
