    "reducedMotion": "The gate is skipped entirely — holding a blank page would be more waiting, not less motion — so `gating` advances straight to `settled` with no idle callback and no timer scheduled, and therefore nothing to cancel. The timeline is never played: the phase effect parks it with `tl.progress(1).pause()`, so opacity, offset and stagger all land on their end frame together because they are all on the one timeline. `leave()` calls the commit synchronously, and a stylesheet rule inside `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` keeps `[data-page-enter]` visible for the frames before hydration.",
