    "reducedMotion": "The manufactured range collapses to one screen and the smoothing is bypassed, so progress tracks scroll exactly. The word passes through at its resting scale with the caption already present — the section becomes an ordinary headline block instead of leaving a screen and a half of empty scrolling behind.",
    "cleanup": "`useRaf` unsubscribes from the shared loop on unmount; the only state is refs. The inline `height` values written to the section and the pin die with the elements, and no observers, listeners or timers are registered.",
    "acceptance": "The word is unreadably large at the top of the section and lands as a normal headline exactly as the section releases. Scrolling backwards reverses it at the same rate. Stopping mid-zoom settles within about a quarter second with no drift. Resizing the window mid-zoom keeps the word at the same progress. With reduced motion on, the section is one screen tall and nothing scales.",
