    "reducedMotion": "The component reads `useReducedMotion` itself and never subscribes to rAF when it is set. All four passes still run, once, at a fixed elapsed of 6.2 seconds, and again after any resize — so the artwork is complete, correctly exposed and fully bloomed, it simply does not drift. A hero background is composition first and motion second; deleting it under reduced motion would leave a hole in the page, and freezing it at t = 0 would show an arrangement nobody designed.",
    "cleanup": "Nulls the stage ref, disposes both `PlaneGeometry` instances, all six materials, and — separately, because nothing traverses them — both render targets. Then `disposeRenderer` performs `dispose` + `forceContextLoss` + a zeroed drawing buffer, and the canvas is removed from the DOM. The canvas is created inside the effect by three and appended per effect run, so a StrictMode remount builds a fresh context rather than reattaching the one that was just force-lost. `useRaf` releases its own subscription; the component adds no listeners of its own.",
    "acceptance": "Three soft coloured lights drift across a dark angled ramp with a halo that is clearly wider and softer than the lights themselves, corners falling off, and no banding anywhere in the gradient — tilt a laptop screen and the ramp stays smooth. Resize the window continuously: the image tracks the box with no stutter, no flash of black, and the halo keeps the same apparent width. Set `reveal` to 0.5 and only the ramp is visible; sweep it to 1 and the lights come up over the last third. With reduced motion the full composition, bloom included, is present and still.",
