    "reducedMotion": "The rAF subscription is never opened. One frame is drawn at `uElapsed = 0`, which parks every marker at twelve o'clock on its ring, so the full structure is visible and only the orbiting stops. Resizing still redraws that frame.",
    "cleanup": "Clears the stage ref first so no queued frame can touch a dead renderer, then `disposeObject(scene)` for the geometry, `material.dispose()`, `disposeRenderer(renderer)` for `dispose` + `forceContextLoss` + zeroing the drawing buffer, and finally removes the canvas from the DOM. The rAF subscription is released by `useRaf` on unmount.",
    "acceptance": "Five rings of dots with one brighter dot travelling each, all at the same angular rate, the outer rings visibly dimmer than the inner ones. Resize the container and the rings rescale without flicker or a dropped context. Zoom the browser to 200% and the dots stay the same apparent brightness rather than getting denser. With reduced motion on, the rings render fully and the markers sit still at the top.",
