    "reducedMotion": "The overlay still appears and the ceiling still applies — withholding content is a behaviour, not an animation, so it is not skipped. What goes away is the motion: the floor collapses to 0 so nothing is held longer than it must be, the removal delay drops to 0 and the CSS transition to 1ms, and the scanning bar becomes a static full-width rule via `animation: none; transform: scaleX(1)` rather than a pulsing one. The result is a brief still plate, not a zero-duration version of the animated one.",
    "cleanup": "Every timeout is pushed into a ref array and cleared on unmount, the ceiling effect clears its own id, and the one-shot `load` listener is removed by its effect. Because the removal timer is cleared, `setPhase` cannot run on a dead component and `onDone` cannot fire for a page that has already gone. No rAF, no observers, no global state beyond the session flag.",
