    "reducedMotion": "Renders a single, un-cloned content set with no tween created at all. The content is fully visible and static — the strip is not left mid-translation and nothing is clipped out of view.",
    "cleanup": "The build effect clears the tween ref, calls `gsap.killTweensOf(tween)` to catch in-flight hover `timeScale` ramps that target the tween object, then `tween.kill()`, then `gsap.set(track, { clearProps: \"transform\" })`. Both `ResizeObserver` instances are disconnected by their hooks.",
    "acceptance": "Watch the seam for a full cycle: no jump, no blank wedge, no change in spacing as one copy hands over to the next. Put two marquees with very different content lengths side by side and both move at visibly the same speed. Hover and the strip glides to a stop over about a third of a second rather than halting. Switch browser tabs and back, and the strip resumes from where it was rather than restarting. With reduced motion the content is static and readable.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical"
