    "reducedMotion": "A `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` block sets `animation: none` and `will-change: auto`. The element rests at its natural layout position — not at the top of the float — so nothing shifts and no gap appears where the animation used to be.",
    "cleanup": "Nothing to clean up. No listeners, no timers, no animation frames. Unmounting removes the element and its CSS animation; React removes the hoisted `<style>` when the last instance unmounts.",
    "acceptance": "The element rises about 14px, hangs, and settles back over five seconds with no visible tick at the loop point. Add a `hover:scale-110` to the same element and the scale still works while the float continues. Give three instances phases 0, 0.33 and 0.66 and all three are already at different heights on the first painted frame. With reduced motion on, the element sits exactly where the layout puts it.",
    "criticalRegion": "critical"
