    "reducedMotion": "No rAF subscription is opened and one still frame is drawn with `uMorph` forced to 1 and `uElapsed` at 0 — the word fully written and completely still, not the scattered cloud. The typography, the particle grain, the depth cue from perspective point sizing and the colour of the written state are all present; the writing, the drift and the dissolve cycle are what stop. A resize redraws the same still. If the raster was rejected there is nothing to write, so the still shows the motionless cloud instead.",
    "cleanup": "The offscreen 2D canvas has its width and height zeroed as soon as the coverage pass is done, releasing the backing store before the WebGL context is even created. A `live` flag is cleared on unmount so a `document.fonts.ready` promise that resolves after teardown cannot write into a disposed attribute. The stage ref is nulled so an in-flight frame cannot draw into a dying context, `disposeObject(scene)` disposes the point geometry and its attributes, the material is disposed explicitly as well, then `disposeRenderer` performs `dispose()` + `forceContextLoss()` + a zeroed drawing buffer — `dispose()` alone leaves the context alive — and the canvas node is removed. `useRaf`, `useInView`, `useVisibility` and `useResizeObserver` release their own subscriptions.",
    "acceptance": "On entering view the cloud gathers into the word from left to right over about two seconds — watch the first letter finish while the last is still travelling — holds it, then dissolves right to left and repeats. The letterforms are legible and match the page's own font, with no gaps in the stems and no visible pixel lattice inside a stroke. Particles nearer the camera are larger, and none of them pop out of existence at any container aspect ratio. Resize from wide to narrow: the word stays fully inside the frame, keeps its proportions rather than stretching, and the particles get smaller with it instead of filling the counters solid. Hard-reload with the cache disabled on a page using a webfont: the word must end up in the real face, not the fallback. Set `text=\"\"` and the cloud keeps drifting rather than collapsing into a blob. With reduced motion the finished word renders immediately and holds still.",
